---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a
          href="/courses/eng-design-fab/"
          class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3"
        >
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Session 12: Program Your Practice Build's CAM</h1>
        <p class="text-sn-theme">Unit 2 &mdash; Manufacturing Foundations, Week 4</p>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Session 12</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Program Your Practice Build's CAM</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>From Your Design to a Real Toolpath</h2>
              <p>
                Session 11 gave you a model. Today, exactly what Session 9
                practiced &mdash; but on your own design instead of a
                provided test coupon.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Same Sequence as Session 9</h2>
              <ol>
                <li class="fragment">Pocket</li>
                <li class="fragment">Drill</li>
                <li class="fragment">Profile &mdash; last, since it frees the part</li>
              </ol>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Nothing New to Learn Today</h2>
              <p>
                Every decision today &mdash; offset, step-over, step-down,
                tabs &mdash; is a skill from Week 3. Today is about applying
                it to something that's actually yours.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Don't Forget Tabs</h2>
              <p>
                Your profile cut fully separates the tray from the stock.
                Session 8's exact reason for tabs applies directly here.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Use Your Session 10 Checklist</h2>
              <p>
                You already wrote a pre-cut checklist. Use it for real,
                right now &mdash; not just for the actual cut next session.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Simulate, Then Simulate Again</h2>
              <p>
                Watch the full sequence run. If anything looks off, fix it
                now &mdash; Session 13 is real material, not a redo.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">This is the last checkpoint before real material.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                A mistake caught here costs nothing. The same mistake caught
                next session costs your actual stock.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">Your own design means your own judgment calls.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Session 9 gave you a shape. Today, you're deciding step-over
                and step-down for a pocket you designed yourself &mdash;
                trust the reasoning, not a guess.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Next Time</h2>
              <p>Session 13: Cut It</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Real material, real machine, everything from four weeks.
              </p>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <h3>Step 1: Set Up the Job</h3>
          <p>Create a CAM Studio Job for your Session 11 part. Select the correct stock and material.</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 2: Program Pocket and Drill</h3>
          <p>Set up your pocket (with justified step-over/step-down) and drill toolpaths first.</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 3: Program the Profile, With Tabs</h3>
          <p>
            Add your profile cut last, using Outside offset. Add tabs so the
            part doesn't come loose at the moment it's fully cut free.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 4: Simulate and Run Your Pre-Cut Checklist</h3>
          <p>
            Simulate the full job. Then go through your Session 10 pre-cut
            checklist against this actual job, item by item.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Before you move on, confirm:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>Toolpath order is pocket/drill, then profile</li>
            <li>Tabs are included on the profile cut</li>
            <li>Your Session 10 pre-cut checklist has been run against this real job, not just filed away</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these on your own. Reflections are individual, even when the rest of the session was team work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>Was setting up CAM for your own design easier or harder than Session 9's provided test coupon? Why?</li>
            <li>You're one session away from real material. Rate 1&ndash;5 how confident you are this cuts correctly first time, then name the single step you're least sure of.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit your CAM Studio file with all toolpaths, your completed checklist run-through, and your reflection.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
